my ADHD brain wants to do everything, so

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.640
if I see a painting, I'm going to be

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.200
like, I want to paint that. Or if I see

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:06.320
a deck of cards, I'm going to surf

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.800
professional poker player. So, we tend

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:09.959
to have a lot of interests, but whether

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.200
we actually do it or not, no tea, no

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:14.320
shade, they make it so easy for you to

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.120
learn actual useful skills that you can

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.880
practically apply to your life, whether

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:19.280
you end up doing it or not. Personally,

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:21.040
I've been exploring some classes around

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.560
creative workflow and digital

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.360
organization, because we all need to

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.959
know the different ways to do things,

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.200
pick out what ever is interesting to us

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:30.519
specifically, and then build our own

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.000
Frankenstein system. But we need to know

00:03:30.519 --> 00:03:33.400
all of these different tools and methods

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.280
that are out there in order to use it.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.280
So, one class I want to point you to is

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.560
this one called Achieve Your Goals. It

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:40.280
walks you through building your own

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.800
goal-setting framework using tools like

